# Day 43

## Experiment Title

Running Automated Tests using GitHub Actions


## Objective

To understand how automated testing can be performed using GitHub Actions workflows.


## Theory

Automated testing is an important part of Continuous Integration. GitHub Actions allows developers to execute tests automatically whenever code changes are pushed to the repository.

Testing workflows help identify bugs and errors during the development process. Automated testing improves software reliability and ensures that application functionality is verified regularly.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Access the workflow configuration file.

Configure testing steps inside the GitHub Actions workflow.

Commit and push the updated workflow file.

Observe workflow execution and testing activity.

Verify the test results displayed in GitHub Actions.


## Output

Automated testing was executed successfully using GitHub Actions.

Workflow execution completed successfully after repository updates.

Test reports and workflow logs were generated successfully.


## Result

Successfully performed automated testing using GitHub Actions workflows.
